## 4) The WORST constraint: `regionTransitGap` (currently very expensive)

Your current approach:

* build `EmpDay` from DaySlot × Seat × Block
* then join `empDayUni` with itself using `lessThan(dayId)` ⇒ **O(M²)** pairs

Refactor it to interval-to-interval comparison:

### Create interval record

```java
static final class EmpInterval {
    final int empId;
    final int start;
    final int end;
    final String factory;
    EmpInterval(int empId, int start, int end, String factory) {
        this.empId = empId; this.start = start; this.end = end; this.factory = factory;
    }
}
```

### Interval-based region transit constraint

```java
Constraint regionTransitGap(ConstraintFactory f) {
    var intervals = f.forEach(CrewSeat.class)
        .join(f.forEach(BlockDecision.class),
            Joiners.equal((CrewSeat s) -> s.blockId, (BlockDecision b) -> b.id))
        .filter((s, b) -> !isUnassigned(s.employee))
        .map((s, b) -> {
            Integer st = seatStart(s, b);
            Integer dy = seatDays(s, b);
            if (st == null || dy == null || dy <= 0) return null;
            int end = st + dy - 1;
            return new EmpInterval(s.employee.id, st, end, s.factory);
        })
        .filter(Objects::nonNull);

    return intervals
        .join(intervals,
            Joiners.equal(i -> i.empId, i -> i.empId),
            Joiners.lessThan(i -> i.end, i -> i.start)   // A finishes before B starts
        )
        .filter((a, b) -> {
            String r1 = CAL.regionOfFab(a.factory);
            String r2 = CAL.regionOfFab(b.factory);
            int need = CAL.transitDays(r1, r2);
            if (need <= 0) return false;

            int gap = b.start - a.end; // days between end->start (inclusive-ish)
            return gap <= need;
        })
        .penalize(HardMediumSoftScore.ONE_HARD, (a, b) -> {
            String r1 = CAL.regionOfFab(a.factory);
            String r2 = CAL.regionOfFab(b.factory);
            int need = CAL.transitDays(r1, r2);
            int gap = b.start - a.end;
            return Math.max(1, need - gap + 1);
        })
        .asConstraint("emp-region-transit-gap");
}
```

✅ This avoids DaySlot expansion *and* avoids EmpDay×EmpDay at day granularity.

